{
	"_comment": "Sea animals (scripts/sim/sea_life.gd), just for looking at: they never affect ships. Each pod spends parts of the year in areas (stays: [area, from MM-DD, to MM-DD], by the in-game calendar), wandering about each, and migrates between them along a sea path the game finds (around land) in the gaps. Positions follow from the calendar alone, so every player sees the same pods and nothing is saved. size is the pod's real number of animals; the map draws at most the species' shown of them. Species: length_px is how long one is drawn (before growing zoomed in), spacing_px how far apart a pod's animals swim, surface (whales and orcas) how often [every s of play, chance] one comes up to breathe and blow, breach how often [every s, chance] one breaches (dolphins: leaps), length_m and fact for its popup. Pod sizes follow the real ones: bottlenose dolphins 2-15 near the coast, spinner dolphins 50-200, orcas 3-5 (transients) to 10-20 (residents), sperm whale family units 10-15 (young males in small groups), and the great whales alone or in twos and threes.",
	"species": {
		"bottlenose": {"name": "Bottlenose dolphin", "plural": "Bottlenose dolphins", "word": "dolphins", "kind": "dolphin", "art": "bottlenose", "length_px": 15, "spacing_px": 11, "shown": 12, "breach": [2.5, 0.3], "length_m": 4, "fact": "They call each other by name: each has its own signature whistle."},
		"spinner": {"name": "Spinner dolphin", "plural": "Spinner dolphins", "word": "dolphins", "kind": "dolphin", "art": "spinner", "length_px": 14, "spacing_px": 10, "shown": 12, "breach": [2.0, 0.35], "length_m": 2.2, "fact": "Famous for leaping clear of the water and spinning up to seven times before splashing down."},
		"orca": {"name": "Orca", "plural": "Orcas", "word": "orcas", "kind": "orca", "art": "orca", "length_px": 21, "spacing_px": 18, "shown": 15, "surface": [6.0, 0.45], "breach": [14.0, 0.12], "length_m": 9, "fact": "Killer whales are really the biggest dolphins; each pod has its own dialect of calls."},
		"humpback": {"name": "Humpback whale", "plural": "Humpback whales", "word": "whales", "kind": "whale", "art": "humpback", "length_px": 32, "spacing_px": 30, "shown": 6, "surface": [9.0, 0.5], "breach": [18.0, 0.28], "length_m": 16, "fact": "Their long white flippers are a third of their length, and the males sing songs that can last 20 minutes."},
		"blue": {"name": "Blue whale", "plural": "Blue whales", "word": "whales", "kind": "whale", "art": "blue", "length_px": 40, "spacing_px": 36, "shown": 4, "surface": [11.0, 0.45], "breach": [40.0, 0.02], "length_m": 30, "fact": "The largest animal that has ever lived; its heart is the size of a small car."},
		"gray": {"name": "Gray whale", "plural": "Gray whales", "word": "whales", "kind": "whale", "art": "gray", "length_px": 30, "spacing_px": 28, "shown": 6, "surface": [8.0, 0.5], "breach": [24.0, 0.1], "length_m": 15, "fact": "Every year they swim about 10,000 miles there and back, one of the longest migrations of any mammal."},
		"sperm": {"name": "Sperm whale", "plural": "Sperm whales", "word": "whales", "kind": "whale", "art": "sperm", "length_px": 30, "spacing_px": 24, "shown": 14, "surface": [10.0, 0.4], "breach": [30.0, 0.05], "length_m": 16, "fact": "They dive over a mile deep after squid, and have the biggest brain of any animal."},
		"right": {"name": "Southern right whale", "plural": "Southern right whales", "word": "whales", "kind": "whale", "art": "right", "length_px": 32, "spacing_px": 30, "shown": 6, "surface": [9.0, 0.5], "breach": [20.0, 0.16], "length_m": 16, "fact": "The white bumps on their heads are callosities, a pattern as unique as a fingerprint."}
	},
